Welcome to the Introduction to Linux day taught by the Bioinformatics core at the [Discovery Research Platform for Hidden Cell Biology](https://biology.ed.ac.uk/drp), today we will go over several different essential topics for using Linux and Linux servers.

During this course you will learn to:

-   Connect to a server
-   Navigate the file system using the Linux command shell
-   Use basic shell commands to view and filter data
-   Look at some basic bioinformatics tools

If you have any questions please contact Daniel Robertson, Heleen de Weerd or Shaun Webb.
